**Compare**: current I = 9 V / (1 kΩ + 2.2 kΩ) ≈ 2.81 mA (the battery's 1.5 Ω is negligible).
- Across the battery ≈ 9.00 V;
- M to GND: 2.2 kΩ × 2.81 mA ≈ **6.18 V**;
- Across R1 (red on the + rail, black on M): 1 kΩ × 2.81 mA ≈ **2.81 V**; with the probes swapped ≈ **−2.81 V**;
- 6.18 + 2.81 ≈ 9.0: around the loop the voltages add up to the battery voltage (KVL).
